      "daily = true for the 1990–2022 daily-resolution events (n=38 in the catalog).",
      "routerCohort reconstructs the backtest's n=33 failed-recovery cohort: the 38 daily events minus 3 router-moot crashes that reached −10% before the 30-td window could resolve (1990 January break, 2018 Volmageddon, 2020 COVID) and 2 echo events without an independent router window (1997 Asia echo, 2000 January break).",
      "routerOutcome encodes the documented cohort split — 14 clean recoveries of which 1 extended ≥10% (7%), 19 failed recoveries of which 11 extended ≥10% (58%). Per-event outcomes are reconstruction (the study reports aggregates); the aggregate statistics are the regression target.",
      "Replaying REAL daily closes (scripts/replay-real) supersedes this reconstruction whenever a daily S&P close series is provided."
    ]
